course: dictionary
lesson: 15717
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «The tract of forest stretched over the hills for miles.» The clue is stretched for miles, so tract must mean a large area of land.
explain: «The doctor checked his respiratory tract.» Respiratory is a clue about breathing, so tract here is a long system of connected body parts. Try the meaning in the sentence: the doctor checked his breathing parts, and that still makes sense.
explain: «She handed out a tract about the village flood at the church door.» Handed out and the idea of a flood tell you this is a small leaflet. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A leaflet would. A large field would not.
fact: A tract can mean a large area of land or water.
fact: In the body, a tract is a long system of connected parts, such as the digestive tract.
fact: «The digestive tract» includes the food pipe, stomach and intestines.
fact: «The respiratory tract» includes the nose, windpipe and lungs.
fact: A tract can also be a short booklet or leaflet that tries to persuade people, often about religion or politics.
exercise: «The tract of forest stretched over the hills for miles.» What does tract mean here? | *A large area of land | A short leaflet | A part of the body | A kind of tree
exercise: «Food moves through the digestive tract.» Which parts are in the digestive tract? | *Food pipe, stomach and intestines | Nose, windpipe and lungs | Arms and legs | Eyes and ears
exercise: Mia found a tract on the bus. What is a tract? | A small river that runs into the sea | A type of cloud | *A short booklet that tries to persuade people | A train ticket for a long journey
test: «The respiratory tract includes the nose, windpipe and lungs.» Which body job is this tract for? | Moving the legs | Hearing sounds | Digesting food | *Breathing
test: «The vicar gave every family a religious tract.» What is a religious tract? | A type of hymn | *A booklet or leaflet trying to persuade people about religion | A large field for farming | A part of the lungs
exam: Which sentence uses tract to mean a large area? | «The tract of the sick man was checked by the nurse.» | *«A vast tract of desert lay under the hot sun.» | «Her digestive tract was sore after the meal.» | «The tract was handed out at school on Monday.»
